<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Nantes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1460</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a> was founded in 1460 by Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> of Brittany with a bull of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-ii">Pope Pius II</a>, giving the duchy its own university. It taught theology, law, medicine and the arts until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a> closed it in 1793, though its law faculty had moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a> in 1735. The present university was refounded in 1962.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-nantes.jpg" alt="University of Nantes" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pymouss44 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nantes_Universit%C3%A9-ch%C3%A2teau_Tertre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
